  "body": "## Result\n\n6600013 / AMR-065-0013: **unsolved, 5/5**, with a full independent scoped source/proof PASS and additive topological clarification.\n\nThe original arbitrary higher-dimensional low-complexity/rational-cohomology implication remains unresolved. The packet proves a sharp Cartesian-product bound, an approximant-rank obstruction, a stable-image criterion, and a finite-stage covering theorem with explicit finite cyclic examples. An infinite-rank profinite tower lacks a continuous finite-alphabet generator for its specified action and is not an admissible FLC counterexample.\n\n## Important scope and clarification\n\nRational \u010cech cohomology, translational hulls, repetitivity and full aperiodicity are explicit. Finite-to-one maps are not automatically covers, and finite-level complexity constants depending on covering degree cannot be used as one uniform constant.\n\nThe variable-length proper-substitution model uses Perron\u2013Frobenius lengths. A tilewise roof-change homeomorphism connects it to the unit-square symbolic suspension and lifts to all decorated covers. This is not a translation-flow conjugacy and does not silently rescale the complexity claims. The additive clarification is prominent in README and final_review.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll 44 frozen author files and nine review files are unchanged. The audit reads all five proofs and exact primary sources, replays 5,367 author assertions with 173 bindings and four local PDF hashes, and adds 22,728 independent controls. Portable checkers use Python's standard library. Source-free replay reports zero PDF checks unless independent source files are supplied.\n\nFresh main and final author ancestry are preserved. Only the target folder and its own QUEUE status/turn cells change. This is one draft PR, with no merge or release and no raw source redistribution.\n",
